---
import ContentLayout from '../layouts/ContentLayout.astro';
---

<ContentLayout title="Cookie Policy - PasteDownloadApp" description="Cookie Policy for PasteDownloadApp. Which cookies and browser storage the site uses, including Google Analytics and Google AdSense, and how to change your choice." canonicalUrl="https://pastedownloadapp.com/cookie-policy/" breadcrumbs={[{ name: "Home", href: "/" }, { name: "Cookie Policy" }]}>
  <script type="application/ld+json">
    {
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "WebPage",
      "name": "Cookie Policy - PasteDownloadApp",
      "description": "Cookie Policy for PasteDownloadApp. Which cookies and browser storage the site uses, including Google Analytics and Google AdSense, and how to change your choice.",
      "publisher": {
        "@type": "Organization",
        "name": "PasteDownloadApp"
      }
    }
  </script>

  <h1 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl lg:text-[28px] font-semibold text-ink tracking-tight mt-0 mb-6 leading-tight text-balance">
    Cookie Policy
  </h1>

  <div class="text-body text-base sm:text-[17px] leading-relaxed space-y-4 [&_h2]:text-ink [&_h2]:text-lg [&_h2]:sm:text-xl [&_h2]:font-semibold [&_h2]:tracking-tight [&_h2]:mt-8 [&_h2]:mb-2 [&_h2]:leading-tight [&_h3]:text-ink [&_h3]:text-base [&_h3]:sm:text-lg [&_h3]:font-semibold [&_h3]:tracking-tight [&_h3]:mt-6 [&_h3]:mb-2 [&_h3]:leading-tight [&_a]:text-link [&_a]:underline [&_a]:underline-offset-2 [&_a]:decoration-link/30 [&_a]:transition-colors [&_a:hover]:decoration-link">
    <p><strong>Last updated:</strong> September 2026</p>

    <p>
      This page explains which cookies and similar browser storage pastedownloadapp.com uses, why, and how you can change your choice. It supplements our <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a>, which covers how the site handles data more generally.
    </p>

    <h2>What Cookies Are</h2>
    <p>
      Cookies are small text files a website stores in your browser so it can recognize the browser on a later visit. Sites also use similar technologies, such as local storage, which keeps a small amount of data in your browser without sending it to a server with every request. This policy uses "cookies" to cover both, and lists each one separately below.
    </p>

    <h2>Images You Paste Are Never Stored</h2>
    <p>
      The paste tool itself does not use cookies. Images you paste, drop, or convert are processed entirely inside your browser and are never uploaded to our servers or saved in cookies or browser storage.
    </p>

    <h2>Your Choice on the Cookie Banner</h2>
    <p>
      On your first visit, a banner asks you to choose <strong>Accept all</strong> or <strong>Reject non-essential</strong>. Until you choose, Google Analytics and Google advertising run with storage turned off, using Google Consent Mode: they are told not to read or write analytics or advertising cookies. If you choose Reject non-essential, they stay that way. If you choose Accept all, analytics and advertising cookies are allowed, and ads may be personalized based on your visits to this and other sites.
    </p>

    <div class="rounded-xl border border-hairline bg-canvas-soft p-4 sm:p-5">
      <p class="!m-0 text-ink font-semibold">Change your cookie choice</p>
      <p class="!m-0 mt-1 text-sm">Opens the cookie banner again so you can accept or reject non-essential cookies.</p>
      <button
        type="button"
        id="openCookieSettings"
        class="mt-3 bg-ink dark:bg-white text-on-primary dark:text-black text-sm font-medium px-4 py-2 rounded-full hover:opacity-90 transition-opacity border-none cursor-pointer focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-link focus-visible:outline-none"
      >
        Cookie settings
      </button>
    </div>

    <h2>Essential Browser Storage</h2>
    <p>
      These items are stored in your browser's local storage, not as cookies. They never leave your device, are not shared with anyone, and are needed for the site to remember your choices. They stay until you clear your browser's site data.
    </p>
    <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-hairline">
      <table class="w-full text-left text-sm">
        <thead class="bg-canvas-soft text-ink">
          <tr>
            <th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold">Name</th>
            <th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold">Purpose</th>
            <th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold">Duration</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody class="divide-y divide-hairline">
          <tr>
            <td class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-ink"><code>cookie-consent</code></td>
            <td class="px-4 py-3">Remembers whether you chose Accept all or Reject non-essential, so the banner does not appear on every page.</td>
            <td class="px-4 py-3">Until you clear site data or change your choice</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-ink"><code>theme</code></td>
            <td class="px-4 py-3">Remembers whether you picked the light, dark, or system color theme.</td>
            <td class="px-4 py-3">Until you clear site data</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h2>Analytics Cookies (Google Analytics)</h2>
    <p>
      We use Google Analytics to understand how many people use the site, which pages they visit, and how they arrive, so we can improve the tool and guides. These cookies are only set if you choose Accept all. Google Analytics commonly sets:
    </p>
    <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-hairline">
      <table class="w-full text-left text-sm">
        <thead class="bg-canvas-soft text-ink">
          <tr>
            <th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold">Name</th>
            <th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold">Purpose</th>
            <th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold">Duration</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody class="divide-y divide-hairline">
          <tr>
            <td class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-ink"><code>_ga</code></td>
            <td class="px-4 py-3">Distinguishes one visitor's browser from another for counting visitors.</td>
            <td class="px-4 py-3">Up to 2 years</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-ink"><code>_ga_&lt;ID&gt;</code></td>
            <td class="px-4 py-3">Keeps track of the current session for the site's Analytics property.</td>
            <td class="px-4 py-3">Up to 2 years</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>
      Google describes how it uses this data in <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">How Google uses information from sites or apps that use our services</a>. You can also install the <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Analytics opt-out browser add-on</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Advertising Cookies (Google AdSense)</h2>
    <p>
      The site is funded by ads served through Google AdSense. Google and its partners, as third-party vendors, use cookies to serve ads, limit how often you see the same ad, measure ad performance, and prevent fraud. With your consent, they may also personalize ads based on your visits to this and other websites. This includes the DoubleClick DART cookie. Cookies Google commonly uses for this include:
    </p>
    <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-hairline">
      <table class="w-full text-left text-sm">
        <thead class="bg-canvas-soft text-ink">
          <tr>
            <th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold">Name</th>
            <th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold">Set by</th>
            <th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold">Purpose</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody class="divide-y divide-hairline">
          <tr>
            <td class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-ink"><code>__gads</code>, <code>__gpi</code></td>
            <td class="px-4 py-3">Google (on pastedownloadapp.com)</td>
            <td class="px-4 py-3">Ad delivery, frequency capping, and measurement on this site.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-ink"><code>__eoi</code></td>
            <td class="px-4 py-3">Google (on pastedownloadapp.com)</td>
            <td class="px-4 py-3">Security and fraud prevention for ads.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-ink"><code>IDE</code>, <code>DSID</code></td>
            <td class="px-4 py-3">Google (on doubleclick.net)</td>
            <td class="px-4 py-3">The DART cookie family: ad personalization and measurement across sites.</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>
      Google changes the exact cookies and their lifetimes over time, and typically keeps advertising cookies for around 13 months in the European Economic Area and the United Kingdom, and up to 24 months elsewhere. The current, authoritative list is in <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/cookies" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google's cookie policy</a>. Other certified ad partners may also set cookies when they serve an ad through AdSense.
    </p>
    <p>
      You can turn off personalized ads from Google at any time in <a href="https://adssettings.google.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google's Ad Settings</a>, and opt out of many third-party vendors' personalized advertising at <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">aboutads.info</a> or, in Europe, <a href="https://www.youronlinechoices.eu/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">youronlinechoices.eu</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Other Third-Party Services</h2>
    <p>
      Pages load fonts from Google Fonts, which receives your IP address to deliver the font files but does not set cookies. The contact form sends your message through FormSubmit, which receives what you type into the form; it does not set cookies on this site. Links to YouTube videos in our guides are plain links, not embedded players, so YouTube sets no cookies unless you click through to youtube.com.
    </p>

    <h2>How to Manage or Delete Cookies</h2>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5">
      <li><strong>On this site:</strong> use the Cookie settings button above to change your choice. Choosing Reject non-essential stops new analytics and advertising cookies from being used, but cookies already set before remain in your browser until they expire or you delete them.</li>
      <li><strong>In your browser:</strong> every major browser lets you view and delete cookies and site data, block third-party cookies, or block cookies for specific sites. Look under Privacy or Site settings in your browser's settings. Clearing site data for pastedownloadapp.com also removes the essential storage above, so the banner will appear again on your next visit.</li>
      <li><strong>Blocking all cookies</strong> does not stop the paste tool from working, since it does not rely on cookies.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
    <p>
      We will update this page when the cookies the site uses change, and adjust the date at the top.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      If you have questions about this Cookie Policy, please <a href="/contact/">contact us</a> or email <a href="mailto:hello@pastedownloadapp.com">hello@pastedownloadapp.com</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</ContentLayout>

<script>
  const openButton = document.getElementById('openCookieSettings');
  openButton?.addEventListener('click', () => {
    const banner = document.getElementById('cookieConsent');
    if (!banner) return;
    banner.classList.remove('hidden');
    document.getElementById('cookieAcceptBtn')?.focus();
  });
</script>
